<title>UK: Transco U.K. gas forecasts for June 7.</title>
<headline>Transco U.K. gas forecasts for June 7.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG Plc has announced the following forecasts and data for U.K. natural gas in the period June 5 to 7.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>June 5 (actual) 150 mcm, 35 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>June 6 (forecast) 150 mcm, 35 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>June 7 (forecast) 141 mcm, 33 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>June 5 (actual) 17.5 Celsius, SNT 14.8 Celsius</p>
<p>June 6 (forecast) 17.7 Celsius, SNT 14.9 Celsius</p>
<p>June 7 (forecast) 17.5 Celsius, SNT 15.0 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption on Friday, with none expected for Saturday.</p>
<p>-London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
